🚀 Day 6 — AWS RDS + Databases + High Availability

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your production database needs high availability with automatic failover. How will you design this using RDS Multi-AZ?

2️⃣ You must scale read-heavy workloads without impacting the primary database. How will you use RDS Read Replicas?

3️⃣ A database migration from on-prem to AWS must be done with minimal downtime. Which AWS tools will you choose and how will you plan the cutover?

4️⃣ Your RDS instance is experiencing high CPU usage. What metrics and configurations will you analyze first?

5️⃣ You need to encrypt all data at rest and in transit for compliance. How will you enable and enforce encryption for RDS?

6️⃣ A developer accidentally deleted data in RDS. How will you restore using automatic snapshots or PITR (Point-in-Time Recovery)?

7️⃣ Your application requires connection pooling because opening DB connections is expensive. How will you implement Aurora Serverless or RDS Proxy?

8️⃣ You need cross-region DR for your production database. How will you design this using RDS Cross-Region Read Replicas?

9️⃣ Query performance has degraded recently. Which logs, metrics, and tools will you use for performance analysis?

🔟 You need zero-downtime upgrades for your RDS engine version. How will you plan maintenance windows and updates?

